        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED",
            "message": "Population Covered",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED_DATE_RANGE",
            "message": "Population covered (For selected date range)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED_DATE_RANGE_FOUR",
            "message": "In other words, we are calculating the total population covered for the selected date range by summing up the population covered for each household within the selected boundary. The boundary data is obtained from MDMS.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED_DATE_RANGE_ONE",
            "message": "In the \"Population Covered\" metric, firstly, we need to know the population data of the household, which can be found in the \"Delivery Intervention\" screen and let us denote it as \"b\".",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED_DATE_RANGE_THREE",
            "message": "For the selected date range, we need to sum up the \"a\" values for all households within the selected boundary (districts for national and provincial level roles, and Administrative Post for district level roles).",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_COVERED_DATE_RANGE_TWO",
            "message": "Then, we calculate the “population covered” for each household by multiplying \"b\" by 1.8, which is denoted as \"a\".",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_TARGETED_DATE_RANGE",
            "message": "Population Targeted (For selected date range)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_TARGETED_DATE_RANGE_FOUR",
            "message": "In summary, the \"Population Targeted\" metric gives an indication of the expected coverage or reach of the campaign, and can help to assess the campaign towards achieving its goals.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_TARGETED_DATE_RANGE_ONE",
            "message": "The \"Population Targeted\" metric refers to the total number of people that are expected to be reached or covered by the campaign during the selected date range. This metric is based on the microplan targets that were set up during the project setup phase.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_TARGETED_DATE_RANGE_THREE",
            "message": "To calculate the population target for the date range, the microplan targets for the province or district are multiplied by the number of days in the selected date range. This gives an estimate of the total number of people that are expected to be reached or covered during the campaign. The boundary data used for this calculation is obtained from MDMS.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_POPULATION_TARGETED_DATE_RANGE_TWO",
            "message": "The population target varies based on the user role. For the national level role and provincial level role, the population target is for the selected “province”, while for the district level role, it is for the “Administrative Posts”.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_SYNC_RATE",
            "message": "Sync Rate",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_SYNC_RATE_ONE",
            "message": "This indicates the percentage of field workers who have synced their device at least once for the current day, i.e. from 12:00AM to 11:59PM.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE",
            "message": "Total Bed Nets Distributed (Cumulative)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE_FIVE",
            "message": "Overall, this metric provides an indication of the progress of the campaign in distributing bed nets to the targeted population.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE_FOUR",
            "message": "The insight is available for this metric which provides a percent change in the number of bed nets distributed between the current day and the previous day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE_ONE",
            "message": "This metric represents the total number of bed nets distributed since the start of the campaign, for the selected province, corresponding province, or corresponding district.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE_THREE",
            "message": "This formula is applied for the entire campaign duration, which is calculated as the time between the campaign start date and the current date.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_CUMULATIVE_TWO",
            "message": "To calculate this metric, the quantity of bed nets distributed to households is captured in the \"Delivery Intervention\" screen of the application and recorded in the \"Quantity distributed\" field. The start date of the campaign is determined during the project setup phase, and the boundary data is obtained from the MDMS.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_CUMULATIVE",
            "message": "Total Households Visited (Cumulative)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_CUMULATIVE_ONE",
            "message": "This metric measures the total number of households visited since the start of the campaign. It is calculated by aggregating all the households visited for the selected province or district since the start of the campaign, depending on the user’s role level. The input fields for this metric include the households visited data which is collected by the Field worker application, the campaign start date from the Campaign project setup, and boundary data from MDMS.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_CUMULATIVE_TWO",
            "message": "This also provides additional insights into the percentage change in the number of households visited from the previous day to today.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_CUMULATIVE",
            "message": "Total Population Covered (Cumulative)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_CUMULATIVE_FOUR",
            "message": "Overall, the Total Population Covered (Cumulative) metric provides an indication of how effective the intervention has been in reaching the target population and meeting the campaign goals.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_CUMULATIVE_ONE",
            "message": "The Total Population Covered (Cumulative) is a metric that shows the total population covered since the start of the campaign, and it is used for monitoring the progress of the intervention in reaching the target population. This metric is applicable for all user roles: national, provincial, and district level, the data will be displayed as per the boundaries permission allotted.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_CUMULATIVE_THREE",
            "message": "Additionally, an insight is available for this metric, which is (Today - Previous day) / Previous Day * 100. This insight shows the percentage increase or decrease in the metric from the previous day to the current day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_POPULATION_COVERED_CUMULATIVE_TWO",
            "message": "To calculate this metric, we use the Population Data for household Covered, which is obtained by multiplying the Quantity of bednets Distributed to the household by 1.8. The campaign start date is obtained from the Project Setup, and the Boundary data is obtained from the MDMS.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_USERS_CREATED",
            "message": "Total Users Created",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_USERS_CREATED_ONE",
            "message": "The \"Total users created\" KPI card refers to the total number of field workers who have been created in the user management module. This includes all field workers who have been assigned to the campaign in a particular province. The total number of staff created and assigned to the campaign is determined by the boundary, which can be at the province or district level. The Dashboard displays the user-created data, based on the user type of the dashboard.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_USERS_SYNCED_ATLEAST_ONCE",
            "message": "Total Users Synced At Least Once",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_USERS_SYNCED_ATLEAST_ONCE_ONE",
            "message": "This key performance indicator (KPI) measures the number of field workers who have synchronized their data at least once in a day using the \"sync tag\" button on their mobile application. The count includes unique syncs from different field workers, and multiple syncs from the same device will only be counted as one. The time frame for a day is from 12:00AM to 11:59PM.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_OVERVIEW_TOTAL_USERS_SYNCED_ATLEAST_ONCE_TWO",
            "message": " It's important to note that if a field worker has synced their data once but after that it has unsynced data, it will not be reflected in this KPI.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REEGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TAB_OVERVIEW_ONE",
            "message": "The \"Registration and Delivery\" section in the dashboard provides information about the field workers who are involved in two different activities: household registration and intervention delivery.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REEGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TAB_OVERVIEW_TWO",
            "message": "The data displayed to the user is totally as per the user role who is viewing:",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED",
            "message": "Bed Nets Distributed",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_FOUR",
            "message": "Overall, this metric provides insight into the effectiveness of bed net distribution efforts within a given area and time period.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_ONE",
            "message": "The Bed nets Distributed KPI shows a bar chart with the total number of bed nets distributed within a selected date range and boundary. The data is collected from the Delivery Intervention Screen in the mobile application, specifically the Quantity distributed field.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_THREE",
            "message": "For the “%” toggle, the metric is calculated as the percentage of bed nets distributed compared to the daily Bed nets Micro plan target for each district or administrative province, multiplied by the number of days in the selected date range.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_DISTRIBUTED_TWO",
            "message": "For the “Number” toggle, the metric is calculated as the sum of bed nets distributed for each household within the selected date range and boundary.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_NOT_DELIVERED",
            "message": "Bed Nets Not Delivered",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_NOT_DELIVERED_ONE",
            "message": "The KPI for \"Bed Nets Not Delivered\" is a measure of the number of households where bed net delivery did not take place within a selected date range.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_NOT_DELIVERED_THREE",
            "message": "The data displayed in the bar chart in the number count for this metric, which displays the total number of households with no bed net delivery for the selected date range, broken down by district or administrative post region, depending on the user's role.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_BEDNETS_NOT_DELIVERED_TWO",
            "message": "To calculate this metric, the data is taken from the application, specifically the count of resources delivered for each household. The total number of households with no bed net delivery is then aggregated and displayed as a bar chart.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED",
            "message": "Households Visited",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_FIVE",
            "message": "For example, for national and provincial roles, the chart will show the percentage of households visited in each district compared to the daily households microplan target. For district roles, the chart will show the percentage of households visited in each administrative province compared to the daily households microplan target.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_FOUR",
            "message": "In the \"%\", toggle the chart shows the percentage of households visited for the selected date range in each district or administrative province, compared to the daily households microplan target and the number of days in the date range selection. ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_MAP",
            "message": "Households Visited",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_MAP_ONE",
            "message": "The \"Households visited\" section in the dashboard provides a map with latitude/longitude coordinates of the households that have been visited within the selected boundary. The map can be zoomed in or out for better clarity of the households.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_MAP_THREE",
            "message": "For district supervisors, hovering over any boundary on the map shows a tooltip showing the name of the boundary and the total number of households covered within that boundary. Clicking on \"+\" or \"-\" will zoom in or out of the map, respectively.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_MAP_TWO",
            "message": "For national and provincial users, hovering over any boundary on the map will display a tooltip showing the name of the boundary and the total number of households covered within that boundary.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_ONE",
            "message": "The \"Households Visited\" KPI in the “Registration and Delivery” dashboard section shows the total number of households visited during the selected date range. The data is sourced from the application.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_THREE",
            "message": "In the \"Number\" toggle, the chart shows the total number of households visited for the selected date range in each district or administrative province. I.e. For national and provincial roles, the chart will show the total number of households visited in each district. For district roles, the chart will show the total number of households visited in each administrative province.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_HOUSEHOLDS_VISITED_TWO",
            "message": "This section includes a bar chart that displays the aggregate of all households visited within the selected boundary. The chart can be toggled between two options: \"Number\" and \"%\".",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS",
            "message": "Planned vs Actual Campaign Progress",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_BEDNETS",
            "message": "Planned vs Actual Campaign Progress (Bed nets)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_BEDNETS_ONE",
            "message": "The Planned vs Actual Campaign Progression (Bednets) chart displays the comparison of bed nets distributed, showing the planned and actual distribution over time. The chart also extrapolates the graph to show when the bed nets distribution will meet the target. The data for bed nets distributed is taken from the Delivery Intervention Screen's 'Quantity distributed' field, and the target bed nets from the Micro plan.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_BEDNETS_TWO",
            "message": "For the planned line, the cumulative 'Quantity distributed' for the assigned boundary is used, and for the actual line, the 'Quantity distributed' for the date range is used. To calculate the X-intercept, the bed nets targeted to distribute per day for assigned boundary or district is multiplied by the number of days in the date range (Campaign start date - TODAY). Finally, the interval for the x-axis is kept for every 1 day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD",
            "message": "Planned vs Actual Campaign Progress (Household)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD_FIVE",
            "message": "The interval for the X-axis is kept for every 1 day, meaning that each point on the chart represents the progress made in one day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD_FOUR",
            "message": "To calculate the X-intercept of the “planned” line, the number of households targeted to visit per day for the assigned boundary is multiplied by the number of days in the date range (Campaign start date - TODAY). For the X-intercept of the “actual” line, the current date is added to the difference between the target number of households and the total number of households visited to date, divided by the number of households targeted per day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD_ONE",
            "message": "This chart is used to track the planned versus actual progress of a campaign to deliver household visits, and to project when the campaign will reach its target. The chart is a line chart with two lines: one for the planned progress and one for the actual progress.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD_THREE",
            "message": "The “actual” line represents the actual number of households that were visited each day, starting from the beginning of the campaign up to the current day. The total number of households visited for each day is used to plot this line. The X-intercept of the actual line shows the projected date when the campaign is expected to meet its target, based on the current rate of progress.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD_TWO",
            "message": "The “planned” line represents the expected number of households that should have been visited each day, based on the micro plan. The cumulative number of households that were targeted to visit each day is used to plot this line. The X-intercept of the planned line shows the date when the campaign is expected to meet its target.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION",
            "message": "Planned vs Actual Campaign Progress (Population)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION_FIVE",
            "message": "The x-axis interval is set to 1 day, meaning that each point on the chart represents the progress made in one day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION_FOUR",
            "message": "The calculation of the intercept is done by dividing the difference between the target population and the actual population covered by the population targeted per day and adding the result to today's date.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION_ONE",
            "message": "This is a line chart that compares the planned and actual campaign progression for population coverage.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION_THREE",
            "message": "The actual data is obtained from the quantity distributed for a given date range. The X-intercept on the chart indicates when the population target is expected to be met based on the current rate of coverage.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION_TWO",
            "message": "Planned data is calculated by adding up the cumulative quantity delivered and multiplying it by a factor of 1.8, representing the average population per household.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
